 # Point One - Critical Reflection
 
-## Reading status — 21 September 2026
+## Reading status — 26 September 2026
 
 This is an earlier research draft, retained for its questions. The current literary argument is in [final.md](final.md); [technical.md](technical.md) now follows the actual encounter.
 
 Some assertions below need revision before reuse. A geometric point does not by itself discretize a continuum or establish a binary classification. The current room does not establish a fixed 90 Hz tracking rate. A position value alone does not record a trajectory, but a surrounding program can record one. Claims about ownership, surveillance and colonial mapping require a particular practice and evidence; they do not follow from the definition of a point alone.
 
-For this hall, begin the critical inquiry in what can be encountered: inheriting a running system; choosing which code to leave unread; locating an undrawn position; giving it a body; naming the frame behind an address; and making different arrivals count as the same event. These are investigative leads, not required conclusions. Preserve the rabbit, pleasure, curiosity and the usefulness of the abstraction alongside its limits.
+The running-system and inherited-work inquiry now opens Point_Zero. Here, begin with absence, a visible surface that permits passage, an identical surface that resists, and a black body that can be held. Then name the frame behind an address and ask how different arrivals count as the same event. These are investigative leads, not required conclusions. Preserve the rabbit, pleasure, curiosity and the usefulness of the abstraction alongside its limits.
 
